// NXP S32K388 — our chip layer.
//
// Inherits Renode 1.16.1's stock `platforms/cpus/nxp-s32k388.repl` and applies
// the corrections we have verified. Inheriting rather than forking means a
// Renode upgrade surfaces here as a reviewable diff instead of silent drift.
//
// What the stock file provides (do not redeclare):
//   cpu0..cpu3   Cortex-M7, cpu1..3 halted at reset (we run single-core)
//   nvic0..3     one NVIC per core
//   program_flash 0x00400000  8 MiB    - where the ELF lands
//   data_flash    0x10000000  128 KiB
//   itcm0         0x00000000  32 KiB
//   dtcm0         0x20000000  64 KiB
//   sram          0x20400000  768 KiB  - Zephyr's main SRAM
//   can0..can7    CAN.S32K3XX_FlexCAN, can0 @ 0x40304000
//   lpuart0..15   UART.NXP_LPUART, lpuart2 @ 0x40330000
//   stm0..3, pit0..3, rtc, siul2, mscm, mc_me, edma
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CORRECTION: SysTick frequency
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The stock file sets systickFrequency: 320000000 on every NVIC. Zephyr's
// S32K344 configuration reports CONFIG_SYS_CLOCK_HW_CYCLES_PER_SEC=160000000
// and drives the ARM SysTick (CONFIG_CORTEX_M_SYSTICK=y).
//
// The firmware computes its SysTick reload from 160 MHz. Renode counting that
// reload at 320 MHz delivers every tick in half the intended virtual time, so
// firmware time advances at 2x virtual time. Measured before this correction:
// a 1 Hz print loop emitted 6 lines in 3 s of virtual time instead of 3.
//
// This matters more here than it would elsewhere. Bench's output is a measured
// reaction latency in milliseconds; a 2x clock error silently doubles or halves
// every number the product exists to report, while everything still looks like
// it works. That is the silent-wrong-answer class this tool must never have.
//
// 160 MHz is the value the firmware actually believes, so it is the value the
// emulator must use.
using "platforms/cpus/nxp-s32k388.repl"

nvic0:
    systickFrequency: 160000000

nvic1:
    systickFrequency: 160000000

nvic2:
    systickFrequency: 160000000

nvic3:
    systickFrequency: 160000000
